# Commit Messages (this repository)

This project overrides the global commit-language rule.

Use **English** for every Git commit in this repo:

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description in English>
```

## Types

Same Conventional Commits types as usual: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `perf`, `test`, `ci`, `build`.

## Rules

- **English**, imperative mood (“add”, “fix”, “update”, “remove”)
- Lowercase after the colon; no trailing period
- One-line subject; body only for complex changes
- Before committing: read `git log -10 --oneline` and match style where sensible

## Examples

```
chore: ignore Thumbs.db in all directories
docs: add pioarduino build instructions
build: add PlatformIO/pioarduino project config
fix(wifi): reconnect after SoftAP fallback
```

## Do not use

```
.gitignore bereinigen
Thumbs.db in allen Ordnern ignorieren
Update files
Fixed bug
```
